/-!
# Explicit short extraspecial families

The shared definitions use the actual `Q1Image` and the fixed source
Golay–Leech comparison. The octad, odd and pure-four families partition all
short elements. Their four source words have explicit minimal Leech
representatives, exact parameter and central-sign identifications, rank-one
tensors and vector corrections. Complementing the octad subset fixes its
group element while negating the representative, as warned in the source.

The octad vectors, odd vectors, `wPlus = v + u` and `wMinus = v - u` span
four mutually orthogonal subspaces. They give an internal direct sum of
the whole short space, with a canonical addition equivalence. The splitting
module documents the source's undefined `R^1` index in the definition of
`B_Z`, interpreted as its octad family `R^2`.

Source: Michael Aschbacher, *Sporadic Groups*, Lemma 27.8, printed p. 150.
-/
